# Walked twin of unit_a3_node_direct_absent.lm2 (--walk-methods: its methods are walked).
# Gate 3, absence (Codex, 2026-09-28, option (2)): `node\name` is a value path into the lexical parent's BODY, never
# into its args part (the signature's descriptors).  The host's formal n is no body field of the host's occurrence --
# only a returned node's copied context carries it (the merge appends it) -- so in a direct call `node\n` reads no
# value: X1 (walk error INVALID), never 0.  A mutant that reads the args part instead would see 0 and exit 0.
fn: makeReader (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    fn: read (int: x) int
        return: node\n + x
    int: e (read: 0)
    return: read

r: makeReader 2
int: a (r: 1)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: a; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
